You will receive a USER'S interaction history (titles + key attributes) and
three deterministic axes already computed from the same history.

Two jobs:

1. Synthesise a compact NL persona — the kind of summary a personal shopper
   would jot down before recommending something. 4–6 sentences, covering
   typical categories / silhouettes / colours, the precomputed price band,
   style direction, materials/brands if visible, and explicit unknowns
   ("price sensitivity unclear", etc.) — do NOT fabricate.

2. Infer the STYLE axis (and only the style axis). Read the item descriptions
   and produce a single style label (e.g. "minimal-casual", "streetwear",
   "preppy", "feminine-romantic", "athleisure", or "mixed" when no single
   direction dominates).

## Precomputed deterministic axes (do not override)
{% for axis in deterministic_axes -%}
- {{ axis.name }}: value="{{ axis.value }}" (confidence={{ axis.confidence }}, evidence={{ axis.evidence | join('; ') }})
{% endfor %}

## History (most recent {{ history[-40:] | length }} of {{ history | length }} interactions)
{% for h in history[-40:] -%}
- {{ h }}
{% endfor %}

Return ONLY a JSON object with this shape:
{
  "profile": "<4-6 sentence NL persona>",
  "preferred_price_band": "<one of: budget, mid-tier, premium-open, luxury-aware, mixed>",
  "style_value": "<style label or 'mixed'>",
  "style_confidence": <float in [0,1]>,
  "style_evidence": ["<short phrase>", "..."],
  "style_secondary_values": ["<optional secondary style labels>"]
}
